Description: Skip the xrdp login window when [Globals] autorun is configured
 Upstream xrdp only skips its login window when the RDP client sends
 autologon credentials (INFO_AUTOLOGON). Microsoft clients only send that
 flag when a password is stored, so a downloaded .rdp file always lands on
 the xrdp login screen on first use.
 .
 Virtua runs one dedicated xrdp instance per VM with a single [vm] session
 whose values are all fixed (ip/port/username/password), selected by
 autorun=vm. In that setup the login window serves no purpose: connect
 directly whenever autorun is set, exactly like the client-autologon path.
 The module-failure path is unchanged: on connect failure xrdp still falls
 back to the login window (WMLS_RESET -> login), so no retry loop occurs.
 .
 Stock configurations (no autorun in xrdp.ini) are unaffected.
Author: AuxiNux Virtua
Forwarded: not-needed
